Posets -- a package for working with partially ordered sets
***********************************************************

Description
===========

This package defines *note Poset: Poset, as a new data type and provides
routines which use or produce posets.  A poset (partially ordered set) is a set
together with a binary relation satisfying reflexivity, antisymmetry, and
transitivity.

Contributors:

The following people have generously contributed code to the package: Kristine
Fisher (see http://www.math.cornell.edu/People/Grads/fisher.html ), Andrew
Hoefel (see http://www.mathstat.dal.ca/~handrew/ ), Manoj Kummini (see
http://www.math.purdue.edu/~nkummini/ ), Stephen Sturgeon, and Josephine Yu
(see http://people.math.gatech.edu/~jyu67/Josephine_Yu/Main.html ).

Other acknowledgements:

A few methods in this package have been ported from John Stembridge's Maple
package implementing posets, which is available at
http://www.math.lsa.umich.edu/~jrs/maple.html#posets.  Such methods are noted
both in the source code and in the documentation.

