adjoinMax -- computes the poset with a new maximum element
**********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        Q = adjoinMax P
        Q = adjoinMax(P, a)
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, 
      * a, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, the new maximal element of $P$
  * Outputs:
      * Q, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, 

Description
===========

This method simply creates a new poset $Q$ with the maximal element $a$.  If
$a$ is unspecified, $1$ or $1$ more than the largest integer vertex is used.

+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : P = poset {{1,2},{1,3},{1,4}};|
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : adjoinMax(P, 100)             |
|                                   |
|o2 = Relation Matrix: | 1 1 1 1 1 ||
|                      | 0 1 0 0 1 ||
|                      | 0 0 1 0 1 ||
|                      | 0 0 0 1 1 ||
|                      | 0 0 0 0 1 ||
|                                   |
|o2 : Poset                         |
+-----------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note adjoinMin: adjoinMin, -- computes the poset with a new minimum
    element
  * *note augmentPoset: augmentPoset, -- computes the poset with an adjoined
    minimum and maximum

