antichains -- computes all antichains of a poset
************************************************

  * Usage: 
        L = antichains P
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, 
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, if specified length of returned
        antichains
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, containing all antichains of $P$

Description
===========

A set of elements of $P$ is called an antichain if no two distinct elements of
the set are comparable.

+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : D = divisorPoset 12;                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : antichains D                                               |
|                                                                |
|o2 = {{}, {1}, {2}, {2, 3}, {3}, {3, 4}, {4}, {4, 6}, {6}, {12}}|
|                                                                |
|o2 : List                                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+

With the input k, the method restricts to only antichains of that length.  In a
*note divisorPoset: divisorPoset,, all chains of length $2$ describe exactly
the non-divisor-multiple pairs.

+-----------------------------+
|i3 : antichains(D, 2)        |
|                             |
|o3 = {{2, 3}, {3, 4}, {4, 6}}|
|                             |
|o3 : List                    |
+-----------------------------+

Since every distinct pair of vertices in a *note chain: chain, is comparable,
the only antichains of a chain are the singleton sets and the empty set.

+----------------------------------+
|i4 : antichains chain 5           |
|                                  |
|o4 = {{}, {1}, {2}, {3}, {4}, {5}}|
|                                  |
|o4 : List                         |
+----------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note chains: chains, -- computes all chains of a poset
  * *note isAntichain: isAntichain, -- determines if a given list of vertices
    is an antichain of a poset

Ways to use antichains:
=======================

  * "antichains(Poset)"
  * "antichains(Poset,ZZ)"

