chain -- generates the chain poset on $n$ elements
**************************************************

  * Usage: 
        C = chain n
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the length of the chain
  * Outputs:
      * C, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, 

Description
===========

The chain poset on $n$ elements is the total order on the integers $1..n$.

+----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : n = 5;                                   |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : C = chain n                              |
|                                              |
|o2 = C                                        |
|                                              |
|o2 : Poset                                    |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C == poset(toList(1..n), (a,b) -> a <= b)|
|                                              |
|o3 = true                                     |
+----------------------------------------------+

It is also the *note divisorPoset: divisorPoset, of a prime $p$ to the $n-1$
power.

+-------------------------------+
|i4 : C == divisorPoset(2^(n-1))|
|                               |
|o4 = true                      |
+-------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note divisorPoset: divisorPoset, -- generates the poset of divisors

