      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, if specified length of returned
        chains
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, containing all chains of $P$

Description
===========

A set of elements of $P$ is called a chain if every pair of elements in the set
are comparable.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : D = divisorPoset 12;                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : chains D                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = {{}, {1}, {1, 2}, {1, 2, 4}, {1, 2, 4, 12}, {1, 2, 6}, {1, 2, 6, 12},   |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     {1, 2, 12}, {1, 3}, {1, 3, 6}, {1, 3, 6, 12}, {1, 3, 12}, {1, 4}, {1, 4,|
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     12}, {1, 6}, {1, 6, 12}, {1, 12}, {2}, {2, 4}, {2, 4, 12}, {2, 6}, {2,  |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     6, 12}, {2, 12}, {3}, {3, 6}, {3, 6, 12}, {3, 12}, {4}, {4, 12}, {6},   |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     {6, 12}, {12}}                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

With the input k, the method restricts to only chains of that length.  In a
*note divisorPoset: divisorPoset,, all chains of length $2$ describe exactly
the divisor-multiple pairs.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : chains(D, 2)                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {{1, 2}, {1, 3}, {1, 4}, {1, 6}, {1, 12}, {2, 4}, {2, 6}, {2, 12}, {3,  |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     6}, {3, 12}, {4, 12}, {6, 12}}                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

