characteristicPolynomial -- computes the characteristic polynomial of a ranked poset with a unique minimal element
******************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        p = characteristicPolynomial P
        p = characteristicPolynomial(P, VariableName => symbol)
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, a ranked poset
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * VariableName => a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, default value q
  * Outputs:
      * p, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the characteristic
        polynomial of $P$

Description
===========

The characteristic polynomial of a ranked poset is the generating function with
variable $q$ such that the coefficient of $q^r$ is the sum overall vertices of
rank $r$ of the Moebius function of $v$.

The characteristic polynomial of the *note chain: chain, of $n$ is
$q^{n-1}(q-1)$.

+--------------------------------------------+
|i1 : n = 5;                                 |
+--------------------------------------------+
|i2 : factor characteristicPolynomial chain n|
|                                            |
|        3                                   |
|o2 = (q) (q - 1)                            |
|                                            |
|o2 : Expression of class Product            |
+--------------------------------------------+

And the characteristic polynomial of the *note booleanLattice: booleanLattice,
of $n$ is $(q-1)^n$.

+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : factor characteristicPolynomial booleanLattice n|
|                                                     |
|            5                                        |
|o3 = (q - 1)                                         |
|                                                     |
|o3 : Expression of class Product                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note isRanked: isRanked, -- determines if a poset is ranked
  * *note moebiusFunction: moebiusFunction, -- computes the Moebius function at
    every pair of elements of a poset

Ways to use characteristicPolynomial:
=====================================

  * "characteristicPolynomial(Poset)"

