compare -- compares two elements in a poset
*******************************************

  * Usage: 
        r = compare(P, a, b)
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, 
      * a, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, an element of the poset
      * b, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, an element of the poset
  * Outputs:
      * r, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether $a \leq b$ in
        $P$

Description
===========

This method determines if two elements are comparable and further if $a$ is
less than or equal to $b$ in $P$.

+-----------------------------+
|i1 : P = poset {{a,b},{a,c}};|
+-----------------------------+
|i2 : compare(P, a, b)        |
|                             |
|o2 = true                    |
+-----------------------------+
|i3 : compare(P, c, a)        |
|                             |
|o3 = false                   |
+-----------------------------+

If two elements are incomparable, then the result is false.

+---------------------+
|i4 : compare(P, b, c)|
|                     |
|o4 = false           |
+---------------------+

