Example: Constructing common posets
***********************************

The standard way to construct a *note Poset: Poset, is the *note poset: poset,
method. However, this package also provides many enumerators for common posets.

For example, we can construct a boolean lattice in many ways. First, we
construct it with the *note booleanLattice: booleanLattice, method.

+--------------------------+
|i1 : n = 3;               |
+--------------------------+
|i2 : B = booleanLattice n;|
+--------------------------+

We can also construct it as a product of length 2 *note chain: chain,s.

+-----------------------------+
|i3 : C2 = chain 2;           |
+-----------------------------+
|i4 : C = product(n, i -> C2);|
+-----------------------------+
|i5 : areIsomorphic(B, C)     |
|                             |
|o5 = true                    |
+-----------------------------+

Further, we can construct it as the *note divisorPoset: divisorPoset, of a
product of primes.

+-----------------------------------------+
|i6 : P = {2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19};   |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i7 : D = divisorPoset product take(P, n);|
+-----------------------------------------+
|i8 : areIsomorphic(B, D)                 |
|                                         |
|o8 = true                                |
+-----------------------------------------+

It is also the *note standardMonomialPoset: standardMonomialPoset, of the *note
Ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal, of squares of the variables.

+---------------------------------------------+
|i9 : R = QQ[x_1..x_n];                       |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i10 : I = monomialIdeal apply(R_*, x -> x^2);|
|                                             |
|o10 : MonomialIdeal of R                     |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i11 : M = standardMonomialPoset I;           |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i12 : areIsomorphic(B, M)                    |
|                                             |
|o12 = true                                   |
+---------------------------------------------+

There are many other common posets that can be generated with this package. See
the below list for the methods.

See also
========

  * *note booleanLattice: booleanLattice, -- generates the boolean lattice on
    $n$ elements
  * *note chain: chain, -- generates the chain poset on $n$ elements
  * *note divisorPoset: divisorPoset, -- generates the poset of divisors
  * *note dominanceLattice: dominanceLattice, -- generates the dominance
    lattice of partitions of $n$
  * *note facePoset: facePoset, -- generates the face poset of a simplicial
    complex
  * *note intersectionLattice: intersectionLattice, -- generates the
    intersection lattice of a hyperplane arrangement
  * *note lcmLattice: lcmLattice, -- generates the lattice of lcms in an ideal
  * *note ncpLattice: ncpLattice, -- computes the non-crossing partition
    lattice of set-partitions of size $n$
  * *note partitionLattice: partitionLattice, -- computes the lattice of
    set-partitions of size $n$
  * *note plueckerPoset: plueckerPoset, -- computes a poset associated to the
    Plücker relations
  * *note randomPoset: randomPoset, -- generates a random poset with a given
    relation probability
  * *note resolutionPoset: resolutionPoset, -- generates a poset from a
    resolution
  * *note standardMonomialPoset: standardMonomialPoset, -- generates the poset
    of divisibility in the monomial basis of an ideal
  * *note youngSubposet: youngSubposet, -- generates a subposet of Young's
    lattice
