Example: Intersection lattices
******************************

The intersection lattice of a hyperplane arrangement $A$ is the lattice of
intersections in the arrangement partially ordered by containment.

+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : R = RR[x,y];                  |
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : A = {x + y, x, x - y, y + 1}; |
+-----------------------------------+
|i3 : LA = intersectionLattice(A, R)|
|                                   |
|o3 = LA                            |
|                                   |
|o3 : Poset                         |
+-----------------------------------+

A theorem of Zaslavsky provides information about the topology of the
complement of hyperplane arrangements over *note RR: (Macaulay2Doc)RR,.  In
particular, the number of regions that $A$ divides *note RR: (Macaulay2Doc)RR,
into is derived from the *note moebiusFunction: moebiusFunction, of the
lattice.  This can also be accessed with the *note realRegions: realRegions,
method.

+-------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : MF = moebiusFunction LA;                    |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : sum apply(LA_*, i -> abs(MF#(ideal 0_R, i)))|
|                                                 |
|o5 = 10                                          |
+-------------------------------------------------+

Furthermore, the number of these bounded regions can also be extracted from the
*note moebiusFunction: moebiusFunction, of the lattice; see also *note
boundedRegions: boundedRegions,.

+----------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : MF' = moebiusFunction adjoinMax(LA, ideal 1_R);|
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : abs(MF'#(ideal 0_R, ideal 1_R))                |
|                                                    |
|o7 = 2                                              |
+----------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note boundedRegions: boundedRegions, -- computes the number of bounded
    regions a hyperplane arrangement divides the space into
  * *note intersectionLattice: intersectionLattice, -- generates the
    intersection lattice of a hyperplane arrangement
  * *note moebiusFunction: moebiusFunction, -- computes the Moebius function at
