filtration -- generates the filtration of a poset
*************************************************

  * Usage: 
        F = filtration P
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, 
  * Outputs:
      * F, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the filtration of $P$

Description
===========

The filtration of $P$ is a partitioning $F$ of the vertices such that $F_0$ is
the set of minimal elements of $P$, $F_1$ is the set of minimal elements of $P
- F_0$, and so forth.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P = poset {{a,b}, {b,c}, {c,d}, {a,e}, {e,d}};|
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : filtration P                                  |
|                                                   |
|o2 = {{a}, {e, b}, {c}, {d}}                       |
|                                                   |
|o2 : List                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+

The filtration of a ranked poset is the same as the ranking of the poset.

+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : B = booleanLattice 3;                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : F = filtration B                                |
|                                                     |
|o4 = {{000}, {001, 010, 100}, {011, 101, 110}, {111}}|
|                                                     |
|o4 : List                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : R = rankPoset B                                 |
|                                                     |
|o5 = {{000}, {001, 010, 100}, {011, 101, 110}, {111}}|
|                                                     |
|o5 : List                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : sort \ F === sort \ R                           |
|                                                     |
|o6 = true                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------+

The *note flatten: (Macaulay2Doc)flatten, of the filtration is a linear
extension of the poset.

+------------------------------------------+
|i7 : member(flatten F, linearExtensions B)|
|                                          |
|o7 = true                                 |
+------------------------------------------+

This method was ported from John Stembridge's Maple package available at
http://www.math.lsa.umich.edu/~jrs/maple.html#posets.

