flagfPolynomial -- computes the flag-f polynomial of a ranked poset
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        ff = flagfPolynomial P
        ff = flagfPolynomial(P, VariableName => symbol)
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, a ranked poset
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * VariableName => a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, default value q
  * Outputs:
      * ff, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the flag-f
        polynomial of $P$

Description
===========

Suppose $P$ is a rank $r$ poset.  For each strictly increasing sequence $(i_1,
\ldots, i_k)$ with $0 \leq i_j \leq i_k$, the coefficient of $q_i_1 \cdots
q_i_k$ is the number of *note flagChains: flagChains, in the ranks $i_1,
\cdots, i_k$.

The flag-f polynomial of the $n$ *note chain: chain, is $(q_0 +
1)\cdots(q_{n-1}+1)$.

+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : n = 4;                          |
+-------------------------------------+
|i2 : factor flagfPolynomial chain n  |
|                                     |
|o2 = (q  + 1)(q  + 1)(q  + 1)(q  + 1)|
|       3       2       1       0     |
|                                     |
|o2 : Expression of class Product     |
+-------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note flagChains: flagChains, -- computes the maximal chains in a list of
    flags of a ranked poset
  * *note flaghPolynomial: flaghPolynomial, -- computes the flag-h polynomial
    of a ranked poset
  * *note isRanked: isRanked, -- determines if a poset is ranked

