flaghPolynomial -- computes the flag-h polynomial of a ranked poset
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        fh = flaghPolynomial P
        fh = flaghPolynomial(P, VariableName => symbol)
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, a ranked poset
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * VariableName => a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, default value q
  * Outputs:
      * fh, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the flag-h
        polynomial of $P$

Description
===========

Suppose $f$ is the *note flagfPolynomial: flagfPolynomial, of $P$.  The flag-h
polynomial of $P$ is the polynomial $(1-q_0)\cdots(1-q_r)f(q_0/(1-q_0), \ldots,
q_r/(1-q_r))$.

+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : flaghPolynomial booleanLattice 3|
|                                     |
|o1 = q q  + 2q  + 2q  + 1            |
|      1 2     1     2                |
|                                     |
|o1 : ZZ[q ..q ]                      |
|         0   3                       |
+-------------------------------------+

The flag-h polynomial of the $n$ *note chain: chain, is $1$.

+----------------------------+
|i2 : flaghPolynomial chain 5|
|                            |
|o2 = 1                      |
|                            |
|o2 : ZZ[q ..q ]             |
|         0   4              |
+----------------------------+

