hasseDiagram -- produces the Hasse diagram of a poset
*****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        D = hasseDiagram P
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, 
  * Outputs:
      * D, a *note digraph: (Graphs)Digraph,, which has the direct edge $(a,b)$
        if and only if $a < b$ in $P$ and if $a \leq c \leq b$ then $c = a$ or
        $c = b$.

Description
===========

The Hasse diagram of a poset is a *note Digraph: (Graphs)Digraph, with vertices
given by the ground set of $P$ and which has the direct edge $(a,b)$ if and
only if $a < b$ in $P$ and there exists no $c$ such that $a < c < b$.

+----------------------------------+
|i1 : hasseDiagram booleanLattice 3|
|                                  |
|o1 = Digraph{0 => {1, 2, 4}}      |
|             1 => {3, 5}          |
|             2 => {3, 6}          |
|             3 => {7}             |
|             4 => {5, 6}          |
|             5 => {7}             |
|             6 => {7}             |
|             7 => {}              |
|                                  |
|o1 : Digraph                      |
+----------------------------------+

Caveat
======

This method renames the vertices with integers $0, 1, \ldots$ corresponding to
the index of the vertices in the *note GroundSet: Poset,.

