hibiIdeal -- produces the Hibi ideal of a poset
***********************************************

  * Usage: 
        H = hibiIdeal P
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * CoefficientRing => a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, default value QQ,
        which specifies the coefficient ring of the *note PolynomialRing:
        (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing, $H$ is constructed in
  * Outputs:
      * H, a *note monomial ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)MonomialIdeal,, the Hibi ideal
        of $P$

Description
===========

The Hibi ideal of $P$ is a *note MonomialIdeal: (Macaulay2Doc)MonomialIdeal,
built over a ring in $2n$ variables $x_0, \ldots, x_{n-1}, y_0, \ldots,
y_{n-1}$, where $n$ is the size of the ground set of $P$. The generators of the
ideal are in bijection with order ideals in $P$.  Let $I$ be an order ideal of
$P$.  Then the associated monomial is the product of the $x_i$ associated with
members of $I$ and the $y_i$ associated with non-members of $I$.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : hibiIdeal chain 3                             |
|                                                   |
|o1 = monomialIdeal (x x x , x x y , x y y , y y y )|
|                     0 1 2   0 1 2   0 1 2   0 1 2 |
|                                                   |
|o1 : MonomialIdeal of QQ[x ..x , y ..y ]           |
|                          0   2   0   2            |
+---------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note hibiRing: hibiRing, -- produces the Hibi ring of a poset
  * *note orderIdeal: orderIdeal, -- computes the elements below given elements
    in a poset
  * *note principalOrderIdeal: principalOrderIdeal, -- computes the elements
    below a given element in a poset

Ways to use hibiIdeal:
======================

  * "hibiIdeal(Poset)"

