hPolynomial -- computes the h-polynomial of a poset
***************************************************

  * Usage: 
        h = hPolynomial P
        h = hPolynomial(P, VariableName => symbol)
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * VariableName => a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, default value q
  * Outputs:
      * h, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, the h-polynomial
        of $P$

Description
===========

Suppose $f$ is the *note fPolynomial: fPolynomial, of $P$, and $d$ is the
degree of $f$.  Then the h-polynomial of $P$ is the polynomial $(1-q)^d
f(q/(1-q))$.

+---------------------------------+
|i1 : hPolynomial booleanLattice 3|
|                                 |
|      2                          |
|o1 = q  + 4q + 1                 |
|                                 |
|o1 : ZZ[q]                       |
+---------------------------------+

The h-polynomial of the $n$ *note chain: chain, is $1$.

+------------------------+
|i2 : hPolynomial chain 5|
|                        |
|o2 = 1                  |
|                        |
|o2 : ZZ[q]              |
+------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note chains: chains, -- computes all chains of a poset
  * *note fPolynomial: fPolynomial, -- computes the f-polynomial of a poset

