indexLabeling -- relabels a poset with the labeling based on the indices of the vertices
****************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        Q = indexLabeling P
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, 
  * Outputs:
      * Q, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, 

Description
===========

This method simply relabels the ground set of the poset based on the indices of
the vertices.

+---------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P = booleanLattice 3;                   |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Q = indexLabeling P;                    |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i3 : P.GroundSet                             |
|                                             |
|o3 = {000, 001, 010, 011, 100, 101, 110, 111}|
|                                             |
|o3 : List                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i4 : Q.GroundSet                             |
|                                             |
|o4 = {0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7}                |
|                                             |
|o4 : List                                    |
+---------------------------------------------+

Clearly, $P$ and $Q$ *note areIsomorphic: areIsomorphic,.

+-----------+
|i5 : P == Q|
|           |
|o5 = true  |
+-----------+

This can be useful for posets whose vertices have unruly names. Note the cache
of $P$ is copied to the cache of $Q$ with the appropriate adjustments being
made.

See also
========

  * *note Poset _ ZZ: Poset _us ZZ, -- returns an element of the ground set
  * *note Poset _ List: Poset _us List, -- returns elements of the ground set
  * *note labelPoset: labelPoset, -- relabels a poset with the specified
    labeling
