isAntichain -- determines if a given list of vertices is an antichain of a poset
********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        i = isAntichain(P, L)
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, 
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, containing elements of $P$
  * Outputs:
      * i, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether $L$ is an
        antichain of $P$

Description
===========

A set of elements of $P$ is called an antichain if no two distinct elements of
the set are comparable.

+--------------------------+
|i1 : D = divisorPoset 12; |
+--------------------------+
|i2 : isAntichain(D, {2,3})|
|                          |
|o2 = true                 |
+--------------------------+
|i3 : isAntichain(D, {2,6})|
|                          |
|o3 = false                |
+--------------------------+

