isBounded -- determines if a poset is bounded
*********************************************

  * Usage: 
        i = isBounded P
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, 
  * Outputs:
      * i, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether $P$ is
        bounded

Description
===========

The poset $P$ is bounded if it has a unique minimal element and a unique
maximal element.

The $n$ *note chain: chain, and $n$ *note booleanLattice: booleanLattice, are
bounded.

+--------------------------+
|i1 : n = 5;               |
+--------------------------+
|i2 : isBounded chain n    |
|                          |
|o2 = true                 |
+--------------------------+
|i3 : B = booleanLattice n;|
+--------------------------+
|i4 : isBounded B          |
|                          |
|o4 = true                 |
+--------------------------+

The middle ranks of an $n$ boolean lattice are not bounded.

+--------------------------------------+
|i5 : isBounded flagPoset(B, {1,2,3,4})|
|                                      |
|o5 = false                            |
+--------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note maximalElements: maximalElements, -- determines the maximal elements
    of a poset
  * *note minimalElements: minimalElements, -- determines the minimal elements
    of a poset

