isConnected(Poset) -- determines if a poset is connected
********************************************************

  * Function: *note isConnected: (Graphs)isConnected,
  * Usage: 
        i = isConnected P
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, 
  * Outputs:
      * i, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether $P$ is
        connected

Description
===========

The poset $P$ is connected if the number of *note connectedComponents:
(SimplicialComplexes)connectedComponents_lpSimplicialComplex_rp, is $1$.
Equivalently, the poset $P$ is connected if between every pair of vertices in
$P$ there exists a chain of relations going from one to the other.

The *note divisorPoset: divisorPoset, of $n$ is always connected.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : isConnected divisorPoset 18|
|                                |
|o1 = true                       |
+--------------------------------+

The disjoint union of any two posets on disjoint vertex sets is disconnected.

+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : C = chain 3;                              |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : P = sum(5, i -> naturalLabeling(C, 10*i));|
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isConnected P                             |
|                                               |
|o4 = false                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------+

See also
