isEulerian(Poset) -- determines if a ranked poset is Eulerian
*************************************************************

  * Function: *note isEulerian: (Graphs)isEulerian,
  * Usage: 
        i = isEulerian P
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, a ranked poset
  * Outputs:
      * i, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether $P$ is
        Eulerian

Description
===========

The poset $P$ is Eulerian if every non-trivial *note closedInterval:
closedInterval, of $P$ has an equal number of vertices of even and odd rank.

The $n$ *note chain: chain, is non-Eulerian for $n \geq 3$.

+------------------------+
|i1 : isEulerian chain 10|
|                        |
|o1 = false              |
+------------------------+

The *note facePoset: facePoset, of the *note simplicialComplex:
(SimplicialComplexes)simplicialComplex_lpList_rp, of an $n$ cycle is Eulerian.

+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : n = 10;                                                          |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : R = QQ[x_0..x_(n-1)];                                            |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : F = facePoset simplicialComplex apply(n, i -> x_i * x_((i+1)%n));|
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isEulerian F                                                     |
|                                                                      |
|o5 = true                                                             |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note closedInterval: closedInterval, -- computes the subposet contained
    between two points
  * *note isRanked: isRanked, -- determines if a poset is ranked
  * *note moebiusFunction: moebiusFunction, -- computes the Moebius function at
    every pair of elements of a poset

