isGraded -- determines if a poset is graded
*******************************************

  * Usage: 
        i = isGraded P
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, 
  * Outputs:
      * i, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether the maximal
        chains of $P$ are the same length

Description
===========

The poset $P$ is graded if all of its *note maximalChains: maximalChains, are
the same length.

Clearly, the $n$ *note chain: chain, and the $n$ *note booleanLattice:
booleanLattice, are graded.

+------------------------------+
|i1 : n = 5;                   |
+------------------------------+
|i2 : isGraded chain n         |
|                              |
|o2 = true                     |
+------------------------------+
|i3 : isGraded booleanLattice n|
|                              |
|o3 = true                     |
+------------------------------+

However, the pentagon lattice is not graded.

+----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : P = poset {{1,2}, {1,3}, {3,4}, {2,5}, {4, 5}};|
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isGraded P                                     |
|                                                    |
|o5 = false                                          |
+----------------------------------------------------+

