isLattice -- determines if a poset is a lattice
***********************************************

  * Usage: 
        i = isLattice P
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, 
  * Outputs:
      * i, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether $P$ is a
        lattice

Description
===========

The poset $P$ is a lattice if every pair of vertices has a unique least upper
bound and a unique greatest lower bound, i.e., every pair of vertices has a
unique meet and a unique join.  Equivalently, the poset $P$ is a lattice if it
is both a lower semilattice and an upper semilattice.

Clearly, the $n$ *note chain: chain, and the $n$ *note booleanLattice:
booleanLattice, are lattices.

+--------------------------+
|i1 : n = 4;               |
+--------------------------+
|i2 : isLattice chain n    |
|                          |
|o2 = true                 |
+--------------------------+
|i3 : B = booleanLattice n;|
+--------------------------+
|i4 : isLattice B          |
|                          |
|o4 = true                 |
+--------------------------+

The middle ranks of the $n$ *note booleanLattice: booleanLattice, are not
lattices.

+------------------------------------+
|i5 : isLattice flagPoset(B, {1,2,3})|
|                                    |
|o5 = false                          |
+------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note isBounded: isBounded, -- determines if a poset is bounded
  * *note isLowerSemilattice: isLowerSemilattice, -- determines if a poset is a
    lower (or meet) semilattice
  * *note isUpperSemilattice: isUpperSemilattice, -- determines if a poset is
    an upper (or join) semilattice
  * *note joinExists: joinExists, -- determines if the join exists for two
    elements of a poset
  * *note meetExists: meetExists, -- determines if the meet exists for two
    elements of a poset

