isLowerSemilattice -- determines if a poset is a lower (or meet) semilattice
****************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        i = isLowerSemilattice P
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, 
  * Outputs:
      * i, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether $P$ is a
        lower semilattice

Description
===========

The poset $P$ is a lower semilattice if every pair of vertices has a unique
greatest lower bound (meet).

Clearly, the $n$ *note chain: chain, and the $n$ *note booleanLattice:
booleanLattice, are lower semilattices.

+-------------------------------+
|i1 : n = 4;                    |
+-------------------------------+
|i2 : isLowerSemilattice chain n|
|                               |
|o2 = true                      |
+-------------------------------+
|i3 : B = booleanLattice n;     |
+-------------------------------+
|i4 : isLowerSemilattice B      |
|                               |
|o4 = true                      |
+-------------------------------+

The middle ranks of the $n$ *note booleanLattice: booleanLattice, are not lower
semilattices.

+---------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isLowerSemilattice flagPoset(B, {1,2,3})|
|                                             |
|o5 = false                                   |
+---------------------------------------------+

However, the lower ranks of the $n$ *note booleanLattice: booleanLattice, are
non-lattice lower semilattices.

+----------------------------------+
|i6 : B' = flagPoset(B, {0,1,2,3});|
+----------------------------------+
|i7 : isLattice B'                 |
|                                  |
|o7 = false                        |
+----------------------------------+
|i8 : isLowerSemilattice B'        |
|                                  |
|o8 = true                         |
+----------------------------------+

