isLowerSemimodular -- determines if a ranked lattice is lower semimodular
*************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        i = isLowerSemimodular P
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, a ranked lattice
  * Outputs:
      * i, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether $P$ is lower
        semimodular

Description
===========

Let $r$ be the ranking of $P$.  Then $P$ is lower semimodular if for every pair
of vertices $a$ and $b$, $r(a) + r(b) \leq r(join(a,b)) + r(meet(a,b,))$.

The $n$ *note chain: chain, and the $n$ *note booleanLattice: booleanLattice,
are lower semimodular.

+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : n = 4;                             |
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : isLowerSemimodular chain n         |
|                                        |
|o2 = true                               |
+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : isLowerSemimodular booleanLattice n|
|                                        |
|o3 = true                               |
+----------------------------------------+

The following lattice is not lower semimodular.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : P = poset {{1, 2}, {1, 5}, {2, 3}, {2, 4}, {3, 7}, {4, 7}, {5, 4}, {5,  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|6}, {6, 7}};                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isLattice P                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : isLowerSemimodular P                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = false                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

This method was ported from John Stembridge's Maple package available at
http://www.math.lsa.umich.edu/~jrs/maple.html#posets.

