isModular -- determines if a lattice is modular
***********************************************

  * Usage: 
        i = isModular P
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, a ranked lattice
  * Outputs:
      * i, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether $P$ is
        modular

Description
===========

Let $r$ be the ranking of $P$.  Then $P$ is modular if for every pair of
vertices $a$ and $b$, $r(a) + r(b) = r(join(a,b)) + r(meet(a,b,))$. That is,
$P$ is modular if it *note isLowerSemimodular: isLowerSemimodular, and *note
isUpperSemimodular: isUpperSemimodular,.

The $n$ *note chain: chain, and the $n$ *note booleanLattice: booleanLattice,
are modular.

+-------------------------------+
|i1 : n = 4;                    |
+-------------------------------+
|i2 : isModular chain n         |
|                               |
|o2 = true                      |
+-------------------------------+
|i3 : isModular booleanLattice n|
|                               |
|o3 = true                      |
+-------------------------------+

The following lattice is not modular.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : P = poset {{1, 2}, {1, 5}, {2, 3}, {2, 4}, {3, 7}, {4, 7}, {5, 4}, {5,  |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|6}, {6, 7}};                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isLattice P                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : isModular P                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = false                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

This method uses the methods *note isLowerSemimodular: isLowerSemimodular, and
*note isUpperSemimodular: isUpperSemimodular,, which were ported from John
Stembridge's Maple package available at
http://www.math.lsa.umich.edu/~jrs/maple.html#posets.

