isSperner -- determines if a ranked poset has the Sperner property
******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        i = isSperner P
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, a ranked poset
  * Outputs:
      * i, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether $P$ is
        Sperner

Description
===========

The ranked poset $P$ is Sperner if the maximum size of a set of elements with
the same rank is the *note dilworthNumber: dilworthNumber, of $P$.  That is,
$P$ is Sperner if the maximum size of a set of elements with the same rank is
the maximum size of an antichain.

The $n$ *note chain: chain, and the $n$ *note booleanLattice: booleanLattice,
are Sperner.

+-------------------------------+
|i1 : n = 5;                    |
+-------------------------------+
|i2 : isSperner chain n         |
|                               |
|o2 = true                      |
+-------------------------------+
|i3 : isSperner booleanLattice n|
|                               |
|o3 = true                      |
+-------------------------------+

However, the following poset is non-Sperner as it has an antichain of size $4$
but the set of elements of rank $0$ and the set of elements of rank $1$ are
both of size $3$.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : P = poset {{1,4}, {1,5}, {1,6}, {2,6}, {3,6}};|
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isSperner P                                   |
|                                                   |
|o5 = false                                         |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : isAntichain(P, {2,3,4,5})                     |
|                                                   |
|o6 = true                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : rankGeneratingFunction P                      |
|                                                   |
|o7 = 3q + 3                                        |
|                                                   |
|o7 : ZZ[q]                                         |
+---------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note dilworthNumber: dilworthNumber, -- computes the Dilworth number of a
    poset
  * *note isRanked: isRanked, -- determines if a poset is ranked
  * *note isStrictSperner: isStrictSperner, -- determines if a ranked poset has
    the strict Sperner property
  * *note maximalAntichains: maximalAntichains, -- computes all maximal
    antichains of a poset
  * *note rankFunction: rankFunction, -- computes the rank function of a ranked
    poset

