joinExists -- determines if the join exists for two elements of a poset
***********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        j = joinExists(P, a, b)
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, 
      * a, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, an element of the poset
      * b, a *note thing: (Macaulay2Doc)Thing,, an element of the poset
  * Outputs:
      * j, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether the join
        exists for $a$ and $b$ in $P$

Description
===========

The join of $a$ and $b$ in $P$, if it exists, is the unique least element
greater than both $a$ and $b$.

+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P = poset {{a,b}, {a,c}, {a,d}, {c,e}, {d,e}};       |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : joinExists(P, b, c)                                  |
|                                                          |
|o2 = false                                                |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : joinExists(P, c, d)                                  |
|                                                          |
|o3 = true                                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : Q = poset {{a,b}, {a,c}, {b,d}, {c,d}, {b,e}, {c,e}};|
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : joinExists(P, b, c)                                  |
|                                                          |
|o5 = false                                                |
+----------------------------------------------------------+

