labelPoset -- relabels a poset with the specified labeling
**********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        Q = labelPoset(P, l)
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, 
      * l, a *note hash table: (Macaulay2Doc)HashTable,, with $P.GroundSet$ as
        the keys and the new labels as the values
  * Outputs:
      * Q, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, a poset isomorphic to
        $P$

Description
===========

This method simply relabels the ground set of the poset based on given
labeling.

+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : P = chain 5;                                            |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : l = hashTable { 1 => a, 2 => b, 3 => c, 4 => d, 5 => e};|
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : Q = labelPoset(P, l);                                   |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : P.GroundSet                                             |
|                                                             |
|o4 = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}                                         |
|                                                             |
|o4 : List                                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : Q.GroundSet                                             |
|                                                             |
|o5 = {a, b, c, d, e}                                         |
|                                                             |
|o5 : List                                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+

Clearly, $P$ and $Q$ *note areIsomorphic: areIsomorphic,.

+-----------+
|i6 : P == Q|
|           |
|o6 = true  |
+-----------+

See also
========

