magnitude -- computes the magnitude of a poset
**********************************************

  * Usage: 
        z = magnitude P
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, 
  * Outputs:
      * z, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the magnitude of $P$

Description
===========

The magnitude of $P$ is the sum over all relations $v \leq w$ of the Möbius
number $\mu(v,w)$.

This integer is multiplicative for Cartesian product of posets, and additive
for disjoint union.

+--------------------------+
|i1 : B = booleanLattice 3;|
+--------------------------+
|i2 : z = magnitude B      |
|                          |
|o2 = 1                    |
+--------------------------+

