ncpLattice -- computes the non-crossing partition lattice of set-partitions of size $n$
***************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        P = ncpLattice n
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the size of the set to
        partition
  * Outputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, 

Description
===========

The non-crossing partition lattice of order $n$ is the lattice of *note
ncPartitions: ncPartitions, of the set $\{0,\ldots,n-1\}$ with ordering given
by refinement.  That is, the non-crossing partition $p$ is greater than or
equal to the non-crossing partition $q$ if each part of $p$ is contained in
exactly one part of $q$.

+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : ncpLattice 3                  |
|                                   |
|o1 = Relation Matrix: | 1 1 1 1 1 ||
|                      | 0 1 0 0 1 ||
|                      | 0 0 1 0 1 ||
|                      | 0 0 0 1 1 ||
|                      | 0 0 0 0 1 ||
|                                   |
|o1 : Poset                         |
+-----------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note ncPartitions: ncPartitions, -- generates the non-crossing partitions
    of size $n$

