orderComplex -- produces the order complex of a poset
*****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        O = orderComplex P
  * Inputs:
      * P, an instance of the type *note Poset: Poset,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * VariableName => a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, default value v
      * CoefficientRing => a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, default value QQ
  * Outputs:
      * O, an *note abstract simplicial complex:
        (SimplicialComplexes)SimplicialComplex,, the order complex of $P$

Description
===========

The order complex of a poset is the *note SimplicialComplex:
(SimplicialComplexes)SimplicialComplex, with vertices corresponding to the
ground set of $P$ and faces corresponding to the *note chains: chains, of $P$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : orderComplex booleanLattice 3                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = simplicialComplex | v_0v_4v_6v_7 v_0v_2v_6v_7 v_0v_4v_5v_7 v_0v_1v_5v_7 |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : SimplicialComplex                                                       |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|v_0v_2v_3v_7 v_0v_1v_3v_7 |                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The minimal non-faces are given by the incomparable pairs of vertices in $P$.
Thus the order complex is the independence complex of the *note
incomparabilityGraph: incomparabilityGraph, of $P$ and the clique complex of
the *note comparabilityGraph: comparabilityGraph, of $P$.  Moreover, the facets
are given by the *note maximalChains: maximalChains, of $P$.  Thus, the order
complex of a *note chain: chain, poset is a simplex.

+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : orderComplex chain 5                 |
|                                          |
|o2 = simplicialComplex | v_0v_1v_2v_3v_4 ||
|                                          |
|o2 : SimplicialComplex                    |
+------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

This method renames the vertices with integers $0, 1, \ldots$ corresponding to
the index of the vertices in the *note GroundSet: Poset,.

See also
========

  * *note chains: chains, -- computes all chains of a poset
  * *note comparabilityGraph: comparabilityGraph, -- produces the comparability
    graph of a poset
  * *note incomparabilityGraph: incomparabilityGraph, -- produces the
    incomparability graph of a poset
  * *note maximalChains: maximalChains, -- computes all maximal chains of a
    poset

Ways to use orderComplex:
=========================

  * "orderComplex(Poset)"

