Description
===========

The rank generating function of $P$ is the polynomial with the coefficient of
$q^i$ given by the number of vertices in rank $i$ of $P$.

The rank generating function of the $n$ *note chain: chain, is $q^{n-1} +
\cdots + q + 1$.

+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : n = 5;                        |
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : rankGeneratingFunction chain n|
|                                   |
|      4    3    2                  |
|o2 = q  + q  + q  + q + 1          |
|                                   |
|o2 : ZZ[q]                         |
+-----------------------------------+

The rank generating function of the $n$ *note booleanLattice: booleanLattice,
is $(q+1)^n$.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : factor rankGeneratingFunction booleanLattice n|
|                                                   |
|            5                                      |
|o3 = (q + 1)                                       |
|                                                   |
|o3 : Expression of class Product                   |
+---------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note isRanked: isRanked, -- determines if a poset is ranked
  * *note rankPoset: rankPoset, -- generates a list of lists representing the
    ranks of a ranked poset

